{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"setlogger","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setLogger"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setLogger"},{"type":"text","value":" is an optional function that allows you to replace the default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"logger"},{"type":"text","value":" used by React Query to log errors. By default, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.console"},{"type":"text","value":" object is used. If no global "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console"},{"type":"text","value":" object is found in the environment, nothing will be logged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { setLogger } from 'react-query'\nimport { printLog, printWarn, printError } from 'custom-logger'\n\n// Custom logger\nsetLogger({\n  log: printLog,\n  warn: printWarn,\n  error: printError,\n})\n\n// Sentry logger\nsetLogger({\n  log: message => {\n    Sentry.captureMessage(message)\n  },\n  warn: message => {\n    Sentry.captureMessage(message)\n  },\n  error: error => {\n    Sentry.captureException(error)\n  },\n})\n\n// Winston logger\nsetLogger(winston.createLogger())","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"logger: Logger"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Must implement the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"log"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"warn"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" methods."}]}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"setlogger","text":"setLogger","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## `setLogger`\n\n`setLogger` is an optional function that allows you to replace the default `logger` used by React Query to log errors. By default, the `window.console` object is used. If no global `console` object is found in the environment, nothing will be logged.\n\nExamples:\n\n```js\nimport { setLogger } from 'react-query'\nimport { printLog, printWarn, printError } from 'custom-logger'\n\n// Custom logger\nsetLogger({\n  log: printLog,\n  warn: printWarn,\n  error: printError,\n})\n\n// Sentry logger\nsetLogger({\n  log: message => {\n    Sentry.captureMessage(message)\n  },\n  warn: message => {\n    Sentry.captureMessage(message)\n  },\n  error: error => {\n    Sentry.captureException(error)\n  },\n})\n\n// Winston logger\nsetLogger(winston.createLogger())\n```\n\n**Options**\n\n- `logger: Logger`\n  - Must implement the `log`, `warn`, and `error` methods.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: setLogger\ntitle: setLogger\n---\n\n## `setLogger`\n\n`setLogger` is an optional function that allows you to replace the default `logger` used by React Query to log errors. By default, the `window.console` object is used. If no global `console` object is found in the environment, nothing will be logged.\n\nExamples:\n\n```js\nimport { setLogger } from 'react-query'\nimport { printLog, printWarn, printError } from 'custom-logger'\n\n// Custom logger\nsetLogger({\n  log: printLog,\n  warn: printWarn,\n  error: printError,\n})\n\n// Sentry logger\nsetLogger({\n  log: message => {\n    Sentry.captureMessage(message)\n  },\n  warn: message => {\n    Sentry.captureMessage(message)\n  },\n  error: error => {\n    Sentry.captureException(error)\n  },\n})\n\n// Winston logger\nsetLogger(winston.createLogger())\n```\n\n**Options**\n\n- `logger: Logger`\n  - Must implement the `log`, `warn`, and `error` methods.\n"}
